TELEGRAM DESKTOP EXPORT

telegram_mcp/tdexport/ is a Python port of the chat export in Telegram Desktop
(https://github.com/telegramdesktop/tdesktop, tag v7.2.10,
Telegram/SourceFiles/export/), Copyright (C) the Telegram Desktop authors,
licensed under the GNU General Public License version 3 with an OpenSSL
exception. telegram_mcp/tdexport/assets/ (css/, js/, images/) is copied
unchanged from Telegram/Resources/export_html/ of the same tag. Both are
included here under GPLv3, the licence of this work, so an export this server
writes is the same as one Telegram Desktop writes.

Photo thumbnails port Telegram Desktop's Qt 5.15.19 scaling and JPEG settings:
telegram_mcp/tdexport/qt_scale.py ports QImage's SmoothTransformation
(qtbase src/gui/painting/qimagescale.cpp and interpolate_4_pixels from
qdrawhelper_p.h), Copyright (C) The Qt Company Ltd., licensed under LGPL-3.0 /
GPL-2.0-or-later / GPL-3.0; the smooth-scaling code there is derived from
Imlib2 (Copyright (C) Carsten Haitzler and others; Daniel M. Duley), under its
BSD-style licence, whose notice is kept here. telegram_mcp/tdexport/qt_jpeg.py
reproduces the settings of Qt's JPEG writer (qjpeghandler.cpp). The encoding
itself is done by mozjpeg 4.1.5 (https://github.com/mozilla/mozjpeg; IJG,
BSD-3-Clause and zlib licences, including the libjpeg-turbo code it contains),
reached through the optional imagecodecs package (BSD-3-Clause); neither is
bundled here.


